course: dictionary
lesson: 12396
title: The word curable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Curable» comes from «cure», which means to make someone well again. The ending «-able» means can be, so curable means able to be cured.
explain: «The doctor said Sam's infection is curable with medicine.» The word tells you that medicine can make Sam well again. Swap in «able to be made well» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Curable is a hopeful word. It tells the reader there is a way to get better. Its opposite is «incurable», where «in-» means not, so incurable means it cannot be cured.
fact: Curable means able to be cured or made completely better.
fact: Curable can also describe a problem that can be fixed or put right.
fact: «Easily curable» means it can be cured without much trouble.
fact: «If caught early, it is curable» means the illness can be cured if people find it soon.
fact: The opposite of curable is «incurable», which means it cannot be cured.
exercise: «The doctor said the illness is curable with medicine.» What does curable mean? | Able to be seen from far away | Very painful and slow | Hard to say out loud | *Able to be cured
exercise: What is the opposite of curable? | *Incurable | Curable again | Easy to fix | Full of medicine
exercise: «The leak is curable if we fix the pipe today.» What could curable mean here? | *Able to be put right | Too big to touch | Already forgotten | Going to get worse for ever
test: «Grandma's cough is curable, so she will be better after her medicine.» Find and copy one word that means able to be cured. | medicine | *curable | cough | Grandma's
test: Which word means the opposite of curable? | Cured | *Incurable | Curious | Healthy
exam: «If caught early, the illness is curable, so the doctor was hopeful.» What does curable tell the reader? | *There is a way to get better | Nobody can help | The illness will last for ever | The doctor is angry
